# Dragon Lava Jump – Cursor Rules

> High-level rules for the editor. **Feature behavior, UI, audio, biomes, and mechanics are specified in `.agents/specs/`.** When implementing or changing game behavior, read the relevant spec file(s) first and follow them.

---

## Specs are the source of truth

- **Feature details** (player, biomes, power-ups, checkpoints, level design, score, UI, audio, cheats, etc.) live in **`.agents/specs/`** as markdown files.
- Use the **index** in `.agents/specs/README.md` to find the right spec. When asked to add, change, or fix something, refer to the corresponding spec and keep behavior in sync with it.
- Update the spec when you add or change a feature so the docs stay accurate.

---

## Project

- **Game logic:** `js/game-phaser.js` (single script, no ES modules). Phaser 3, Arcade physics. Runs from `file://` or a static server.
- **Entry:** `dragonlavajump.html` + `css/styles.css`.
- **Assets:** `assets/audio/` for shared audio; `assets/biomes/<biomeId>/` for biome-specific assets (e.g. `assets/biomes/desert/audio/`).
- **Legacy:** `legacy/` is reference only; do not rely on it for current behavior.

---

## Global rules

- **No license:** This project is not licensed for reuse or distribution. Do not add license files or license sections.
- **Constants:** Physics and layout constants are at the top of `game-phaser.js`; biome-specific ones live with the biome section. Change them carefully.
- **Physics:** Arcade physics. Player hitbox is fixed; do not tie it to facing direction.
